  "i18n": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Skipping at Dusk",
      "concept": "The core is the feel of stone skipping: flick up the instant the stone is level. Each skip rings one note higher, so a good throw becomes a little melody. Clearing lake challenges turns the sunset into a moonlit night.",
      "howToPlay": "When the stone in your hand glows level, flick up fast to throw. The flick direction aims the throw.",
      "libraryDecision": "Uses three.js: a chase camera skimming the water after the stone, with ripples and the sunset glint receding in depth, is the pleasure of skipping itself. The physics is hand-written so the bounces are easy to tune.",
      "soundDecision": "Hand-made Web Audio. Each skip plays the next note of a pentatonic scale, so you hear your count and a long throw becomes a melody. Soft water ambience, a plop when it sinks, crickets at night."
    }
